+### Exact-token SGLang experiments
+
+The patched harness accepts paired `input_ids` and `output_ids` on each normal
+or streaming Weka request. Their lengths must match `in` and `out`. Use
+`--endpoint-type sglang-token-completions` and set `AGENTX_REPLAY_MODE=recorded`
+to send the recorded response IDs to a patched SGLang server. Set the mode to
+`generated` for normal sampling with the same fixed prompt IDs and lengths.
+The endpoint uses `cache_salt` for session isolation, preserves the complete
+prompt IDs, and limits replay IDs to one token for one-token warmup credits.
+It requires token-bearing turns; ordinary completions retain their existing
+capability declaration. Local traces require `--unsafe-override` and produce
+`submission_valid=false`; they are not public-corpus submissions.
+
